LOK: read whether listed commands may run now

LOK pushes enable states only for a fixed list, and only after
idle bindings update. A menu opened right after a selection needs
the answer now, for commands outside that list (hide rows, column
width, clear contents). getCommandValues(".uno:CommandStates?
commands=.uno:A,.uno:B") flushes the dispatcher and asks it for
each slot, as the menu bar would: true unless disabled or unknown
to the current shells. A name that is no slot fails the read.

